[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m4. Test the flows[22m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
In-page dictation:[0m[0m
- Go to Settings → set Ollama URL ([38;5;10mhttp://localhost:11434[0m) and model ([38;5;10mphi4-mini[0m) → hit Test Connection[0m[0m
- Go to Dictation page → it should show green status indicators for both Whisper and Ollama[0m[0m
- If no whisper model is downloaded yet, you'll see the Model Download UI — download one (Tiny English is fastest)[0m[0m
- Hit Start Dictation, speak, hit Stop — you should see raw transcript then processed output[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Hotkey dictation:[0m[0m
- Press F4 → you should hear the start sound and see a macOS notification "Listening..."[0m[0m
- Speak, then press F4 again → stop sound, "Processing..." notification[0m[0m
- After processing: done sound, "Copied to clipboard!" notification, result in your clipboard[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Snippets:[0m[0m
- Go to Snippets page → create one (e.g. trigger: "signature", expansion: "Best regards, ...")[0m[0m
- Dictate "signature" → should expand to the snippet text instead of going through Ollama[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mIf you just want to test the UI without the full pipeline[22m, you can run [38;5;10mnpm run dev[0m (browser mode) — but Dictation/Snippets pages won't appear in the sidebar since they're gated by [38;5;10misElectron()[0m. The Settings page dictation section is also hidden in browser mode.[0m[0m
